1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,390
On July 8, 1947, the public information

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:06,271
office at Roswell Army Air Field, in New

3
00:00:06,291 --> 00:00:09,297
Mexico, put out a remarkable announcement.

4
00:00:09,767 --> 00:00:11,965
The Army, it said, had recovered a flying

5
00:00:11,985 --> 00:00:12,235
disc.

6
00:00:12,805 --> 00:00:14,440
The next day, the papers carried a

7
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:15,219
different story.

8
00:00:15,559 --> 00:00:17,927
A general in Fort Worth, Texas, had said

9
00:00:17,947 --> 00:00:20,315
the object was a radar-tracking balloon.

10
00:00:20,885 --> 00:00:23,033
For thirty years, almost nobody cared.

11
00:00:23,503 --> 00:00:25,449
Then the story came back, bigger than

12
00:00:25,469 --> 00:00:25,821
before.

13
00:00:26,161 --> 00:00:28,190
Stories of strange metal, of a second

14
00:00:28,210 --> 00:00:29,631
crash site, and of bodies.

15
00:00:30,551 --> 00:00:32,394
In the 1990s, under pressure from

16
00:00:32,414 --> 00:00:34,708
Congress, the Air Force went back through

17
00:00:34,728 --> 00:00:35,611
its own records.

18
00:00:36,081 --> 00:00:37,828
It published two official reports.

19
00:00:38,168 --> 00:00:40,369
One offered an explanation for the debris.

20
00:00:40,709 --> 00:00:42,521
The other, for the stories of bodies.

21
00:00:43,091 --> 00:00:45,287
Here is what those reports actually say.

22
00:00:45,627 --> 00:00:47,001
And where they've been challenged.

23
00:00:47,571 --> 00:00:48,844
Let's open the file.

24
00:00:55,171 --> 00:00:56,359
It started on a ranch.

25
00:00:56,979 --> 00:00:59,422
According to the Roswell Daily Record, a

26
00:00:59,442 --> 00:01:00,407
rancher named W.

27
00:01:00,747 --> 00:01:01,401
W.

28
00:01:01,741 --> 00:01:04,511
Brazel, known as Mac, and his son came

29
00:01:04,531 --> 00:01:07,522
across a large area of bright wreckage on

30
00:01:07,542 --> 00:01:08,550
June 14, 1947.

31
00:01:08,890 --> 00:01:11,480
About 75 miles northwest of Roswell.

32
00:01:12,050 --> 00:01:14,078
The paper said it was made up of rubber

33
00:01:14,098 --> 00:01:16,283
strips, tinfoil, a rather tough paper, and

34
00:01:16,303 --> 00:01:16,651
sticks.

35
00:01:17,221 --> 00:01:19,413
In early July, Brazel told the sheriff he

36
00:01:19,433 --> 00:01:21,086
