47
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:43,871
Tape with flowers printed on it.

48
00:01:44,211 --> 00:01:45,383
Eyelets in the paper.

49
00:01:45,853 --> 00:01:48,030
And the whole lot, he estimated, weighed

50
00:01:48,050 --> 00:01:49,019
maybe five pounds.

51
00:01:49,589 --> 00:01:50,931
But he also said this.

52
00:01:51,351 --> 00:01:53,743
I am sure what I found was not any weather

53
00:01:53,763 --> 00:01:54,891
observation balloon.

54
00:01:55,461 --> 00:01:57,803
On July 8, the day of the announcement,

55
00:01:57,823 --> 00:02:00,347
the FBI's Dallas office sent a teletype to

56
00:02:00,367 --> 00:02:01,134
headquarters.

57
00:02:01,604 --> 00:02:04,040
An Eighth Air Force official had described

58
00:02:04,060 --> 00:02:06,438
the object as hexagonal, suspended from a

59
00:02:06,458 --> 00:02:07,432
balloon by cable.

60
00:02:07,772 --> 00:02:09,909
It resembled, he said, a high-altitude

61
00:02:09,929 --> 00:02:12,122
weather balloon with a radar reflector.

62
00:02:12,592 --> 00:02:14,445
But, the message added, a phone call

63
00:02:14,465 --> 00:02:16,577
between their office and Wright Field had

64
00:02:16,597 --> 00:02:17,929
not borne out this belief.

65
00:02:18,499 --> 00:02:20,713
The debris, the message said, was being

66
00:02:20,733 --> 00:02:22,717
flown to Wright Field, in Ohio, for

67
00:02:22,737 --> 00:02:23,404
examination.

68
00:02:23,874 --> 00:02:25,871
No further investigation was being

69
00:02:25,891 --> 00:02:26,464
conducted.

70
00:02:27,035 --> 00:02:29,671
The base's own history for July 1947

71
00:02:29,691 --> 00:02:31,737
settled it in two sentences.

72
00:02:32,077 --> 00:02:34,167
The public information office was kept

73
00:02:34,187 --> 00:02:36,278
busy answering inquiries on the flying

74
00:02:36,298 --> 00:02:36,556
disc.

75
00:02:37,026 --> 00:02:38,921
The object turned out to be a radar

76
00:02:38,941 --> 00:02:39,851
tracking balloon.

77
00:02:40,770 --> 00:02:41,760
And that was that.

78
00:02:42,381 --> 00:02:45,404
According to the Air Force, Roswell wasn't

79
00:02:45,424 --> 00:02:48,230
even treated as a UFO event until 1978.

80
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:51,132
It doesn't appear in Project Blue Book,

81
00:02:51,152 --> 00:02:53,709
the Air Force's official investigation of

82
00:02:53,729 --> 00:02:54,464
UFO reports.

83
00:02:55,033 --> 00:02:57,814
In 1978, a tabloid reported that Marcel,

84
00:02:57,834 --> 00:03:00,335
the former intelligence officer, now

85
00:03:00,355 --> 00:03:03,205
claimed the debris he handled came from a

86
00:03:03,225 --> 00:03:03,485
UFO.

87
00:03:03,955 --> 00:03:06,088
A researcher, Stanton Friedman, began

88
00:03:06,108 --> 00:03:06,902
investigating.

89
00:03:07,242 --> 00:03:09,350
And in 1980, a book called The Roswell

90
00:03:09,370 --> 00:03:10,862
Incident laid out the case.

91
00:03:11,432 --> 00:03:13,462
Over the next decade, the story grew.

92
00:03:13,802 --> 00:03:16,078
More witnesses came forward, many of them

93
00:03:16,098 --> 00:03:18,094
speaking forty years after the fact.

94
00:03:18,564 --> 00:03:20,668
According to the Air Force, the debris

95
00:03:20,688 --> 00:03:22,847
grew from a small area to multiple huge

96
00:03:22,867 --> 00:03:23,629
debris fields.

97
00:03:23,969 --> 00:03:26,426
Sticks and tinfoil became exotic metals.

98
00:03:26,996 --> 00:03:29,133
And most versions now included a second

99
00:03:29,153 --> 00:03:31,234
site, where, it was said, the military

100
00:03:31,254 --> 00:03:33,501
recovered bodies, and flew them to Wright

101
00:03:33,521 --> 00:03:33,832
Field.

102
00:03:34,752 --> 00:03:36,393
Which is where Congress came in.

103
00:03:37,013 --> 00:03:39,616
In 1993, New Mexico Congressman Steven

104
00:03:39,636 --> 00:03:42,377
Schiff asked the Pentagon about Roswell.

105
00:03:42,717 --> 00:03:44,544
He felt he was given the runaround.

106
00:03:45,114 --> 00:03:47,656
In January 1994, he told the Washington

107
00:03:47,676 --> 00:03:49,889
Post, whatever it was, it wasn't a

108
00:03:49,909 --> 00:03:50,414
balloon.

109
00:03:50,754 --> 00:03:52,628
Apparently, it's another government

110
00:03:52,648 --> 00:03:53,061
coverup.

111
00:03:53,632 --> 00:03:55,721
At his request, the General Accounting

112
00:03:55,741 --> 00:03:58,053
Office, the investigative arm of Congress,

113
00:03:58,073 --> 00:03:58,942
opened an audit.

114
00:03:59,412 --> 00:04:01,448
And the Air Force launched its own search.

115
00:04:02,018 --> 00:04:04,353
Its researchers went through archives and

116
00:04:04,373 --> 00:04:06,364
records centers across the country,

117
00:04:06,384 --> 00:04:07,915
including Top Secret files.

118
00:04:08,385 --> 00:04:10,648
Any current or former Air Force official

119
00:04:10,668 --> 00:04:12,818
bound by a secrecy oath, the Air Force

120
00:04:12,838 --> 00:04:14,474
said, would be freed from it.

121
00:04:15,044 --> 00:04:17,801
In July 1994, Colonel Richard Weaver sent

122
00:04:17,821 --> 00:04:20,374
the result to the Secretary of the Air

123
00:04:20,394 --> 00:04:20,781
Force.

124
00:04:21,363 --> 00:04:23,842
The search, he wrote, did not identify any

125
00:04:23,862 --> 00:04:26,223
indication that the Roswell Incident was

126
00:04:26,243 --> 00:04:28,306
any type of extraterrestrial event.

127
00:04:28,875 --> 00:04:31,457
Nor that the Air Force had engaged in a

128
00:04:31,477 --> 00:04:32,724
47-year conspiracy.

129
00:04:33,194 --> 00:04:35,059
He predicted what would happen next.

130
00:04:35,399 --> 00:04:37,293
Critics, he wrote, would denounce the

131
00:04:37,313 --> 00:04:39,413
report as a continuation of the cover-up.

132
00:04:40,334 --> 00:04:42,226
So what did the Air Force say actually

133
00:04:42,246 --> 00:04:43,132
fell on the ranch?

134
00:04:43,752 --> 00:04:44,476
A balloon.

135
00:04:44,816 --> 00:04:46,691
But not an ordinary weather balloon.

136
00:04:47,161 --> 00:04:49,195
The answer, the report said, had been

137
00:04:49,215 --> 00:04:50,472
declassified for years.

138
00:04:50,812 --> 00:04:53,362
A formerly Top Secret project, code-named

139
00:04:53,382 --> 00:04:53,738
Mogul.

140
00:04:54,308 --> 00:04:56,475
After World War II, the United States

141
00:04:56,495 --> 00:04:58,603
needed to know when the Soviet Union

142
00:04:58,623 --> 00:05:00,317
tested its first atomic bomb.

143
00:05:00,657 --> 00:05:02,319
The Soviet borders were closed.

144
00:05:02,789 --> 00:05:04,910
Mogul's idea was to listen for it.

145
00:05:05,250 --> 00:05:07,517
Acoustic sensors, carried high into the

146
00:05:07,537 --> 00:05:09,746
atmosphere by balloons, to pick up the

147
00:05:09,766 --> 00:05:11,857
low-frequency sound waves of distant

148
00:05:11,877 --> 00:05:12,502
explosions.

149
00:05:13,072 --> 00:05:14,900
The balloons flew in long trains.

150
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:17,671
According to the Air Force, more than 600

151
00:05:17,691 --> 00:05:19,824
feet of balloons, sensors, and radar

152
00:05:19,844 --> 00:05:22,155
reflectors, strung together on a single

153
00:05:22,175 --> 00:05:22,454
line.

154
00:05:23,024 --> 00:05:24,873
The radar reflectors were the key.

155
00:05:25,213 --> 00:05:27,502
Foil-covered paper on balsa-wood sticks,

156
00:05:27,522 --> 00:05:29,291
held with tape, glue and twine.

157
00:05:29,761 --> 00:05:31,799
According to the project's engineer,

158
00:05:31,819 --> 00:05:33,971
Charles Moore, some early targets were

159
00:05:33,991 --> 00:05:36,086
made by a toy or novelty company, and

160
00:05:36,106 --> 00:05:38,430
assembled with purplish-pink tape printed

161
00:05:38,450 --> 00:05:39,173
with symbols.

162
00:05:39,743 --> 00:05:41,642
A former project officer, Albert

163
00:05:41,662 --> 00:05:43,741
Trakowski, described that tape too.

164
00:05:44,081 --> 00:05:45,184
Flowers and hearts.

165
00:05:45,754 --> 00:05:48,473
New York University's team launched the

166
00:05:48,493 --> 00:05:51,142
Mogul flights from Alamogordo Army Air

167
00:05:51,162 --> 00:05:53,812
Field, in New Mexico, starting in June

168
00:05:53,832 --> 00:05:54,163
1947.

169
00:05:54,503 --> 00:05:56,213
Some of the early flights were never

170
00:05:56,233 --> 00:05:56,549
logged.

171
00:05:57,119 --> 00:05:59,845
One of them, Flight 4, went up on June 4,

172
00:05:59,865 --> 00:06:02,324
1947, according to the journal of the

173
00:06:02,344 --> 00:06:04,333
field scientist, Albert Crary.

174
00:06:04,803 --> 00:06:07,207
It was not recovered by the N Y U group.

175
00:06:07,777 --> 00:06:10,165
Ten days later, Brazel found his wreckage.

176
00:06:10,635 --> 00:06:12,974
In Moore's scientific opinion, the debris

177
00:06:12,994 --> 00:06:14,814
was most probably from Flight 4.

178
00:06:15,384 --> 00:06:17,610
The Air Force also found the last living

179
00:06:17,630 --> 00:06:19,351
one of the three men officially

180
00:06:19,371 --> 00:06:21,541
acknowledged to have recovered material

181
00:06:21,561 --> 00:06:23,450
from the ranch: Sheridan Cavitt, a

182
00:06:23,470 --> 00:06:25,584
counterintelligence agent who went out

183
00:06:25,604 --> 00:06:26,257
with Marcel.

184
00:06:26,827 --> 00:06:29,114
In a sworn statement, he described bamboo

185
00:06:29,134 --> 00:06:31,363
type square sticks, very light, and some

186
00:06:31,383 --> 00:06:33,444
sort of metallic reflecting material.

187
00:06:33,914 --> 00:06:36,010
I remember, he said, recognizing this

188
00:06:36,030 --> 00:06:38,012
material as being consistent with a

189
00:06:38,032 --> 00:06:38,926
weather balloon.

190
00:06:39,496 --> 00:06:41,393
The report's conclusion was careful.

191
00:06:41,733 --> 00:06:44,009
The most likely source of the wreckage was

192
00:06:44,029 --> 00:06:46,195
one of the Project Mogul balloon trains.

193
00:06:46,665 --> 00:06:48,697
The flying disc announcement, it said,

194
00:06:48,717 --> 00:06:50,802
seemed to be an overreaction, at a time

195
00:06:50,822 --> 00:06:52,907
when nobody knew for sure what the term

196
00:06:52,927 --> 00:06:53,501
even meant.

197
00:06:54,421 --> 00:06:56,451
But Mogul couldn't explain the bodies.

198
00:06:57,071 --> 00:07:00,513
On June 24, 1997, the Air Force released a

199
00:07:00,533 --> 00:07:01,667
second report.

200
00:07:02,007 --> 00:07:04,092
Its title: The Roswell Report, Case

201
00:07:04,112 --> 00:07:04,512
Closed.

202
00:07:05,082 --> 00:07:07,506
Its central claim was that the accounts of

203
00:07:07,526 --> 00:07:09,601
bodies, in most instances, described

204
00:07:09,621 --> 00:07:11,230
actual Air Force activities.

205
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:14,528
But those activities hadn't happened in

206
00:07:14,548 --> 00:07:14,893
1947.

207
00:07:15,463 --> 00:07:18,300
From 1953 to 1959, Air Force scientists

208
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:21,303
studied how a pilot could survive bailing

209
00:07:21,323 --> 00:07:23,061
out at extreme altitude.

210
00:07:23,531 --> 00:07:25,930
To test it, they used human-sized dummies.

211
00:07:26,499 --> 00:07:29,390
The report counts 43 balloon flights

212
00:07:29,410 --> 00:07:32,462
carrying 67 dummies across New Mexico,

213
00:07:32,482 --> 00:07:35,372
between June 1954 and February 1959.

214
00:07:35,842 --> 00:07:38,361
Most came down outside military land, in

215
00:07:38,381 --> 00:07:40,709
eastern New Mexico, near Roswell, and

216
00:07:40,729 --> 00:07:42,422
around the Tularosa Valley.

217
00:07:42,992 --> 00:07:44,833
The recovery crews, the report says,

218
00:07:44,853 --> 00:07:46,900
arrived fast, in trucks and aircraft, to

219
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:49,070
collect the dummies and their instruments.

220
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:51,509
That, it says, explains stories of

221
00:07:51,529 --> 00:07:53,614
military units arriving just after a

222
00:07:53,634 --> 00:07:53,965
crash.

223
00:07:54,535 --> 00:07:56,524
The claims about bodies at the base

224
00:07:56,544 --> 00:07:58,704
hospital, the report said, most likely

225
00:07:58,724 --> 00:08:00,368
combined two separate events.

226
00:08:00,838 --> 00:08:03,627
A 1956 aircraft accident in which eleven

227
00:08:03,647 --> 00:08:06,084
Air Force members lost their lives.

228
00:08:06,424 --> 00:08:09,183
And a 1959 balloon mishap in which two Air

229
00:08:09,203 --> 00:08:10,903
Force pilots were injured.

230
00:08:11,473 --> 00:08:12,586
Its conclusion.

231
00:08:13,006 --> 00:08:15,638
Air Force activities over many years had

232
00:08:15,658 --> 00:08:17,694
been consolidated, and were now

233
00:08:17,714 --> 00:08:20,213
represented to have occurred in two or

234
00:08:20,233 --> 00:08:21,804
three days in July 1947.

235
00:08:22,724 --> 00:08:24,527
And that is exactly where the critics

236
00:08:24,547 --> 00:08:25,117
pushed back.

237
00:08:25,737 --> 00:08:27,239
The problem was obvious.

238
00:08:27,579 --> 00:08:30,751
The dummy drops began years after 1947.

239
00:08:31,221 --> 00:08:33,671
Stanton Friedman told reporters that none

240
00:08:33,691 --> 00:08:36,019
of that work was done before the 1950s.

241
00:08:36,359 --> 00:08:38,475
Another researcher, Karl Pflock, who

242
00:08:38,495 --> 00:08:40,966
accepted the Mogul explanation, called the

243
00:08:40,986 --> 00:08:42,923
dummy explanation a real stretch.

244
00:08:43,493 --> 00:08:45,827
At the Pentagon briefing, according to the

245
00:08:45,847 --> 00:08:47,900
Spokesman-Review, Colonel John Haynes

246
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:49,917
answered that when people talk about

247
00:08:49,937 --> 00:08:52,158
things over a period of time, they begin

248
00:08:52,178 --> 00:08:54,062
to lose exactly when the date was.

249
00:08:54,632 --> 00:08:55,734
There were other gaps.

250
00:08:56,074 --> 00:08:59,422
The GAO found that records of the base's

251
00:08:59,442 --> 00:09:02,957
administrative activity from 1945 to 1949,

252
00:09:02,977 --> 00:09:06,324
and its outgoing messages from late 1946

253
00:09:06,344 --> 00:09:08,681
to 1949, had been destroyed.

254
00:09:09,251 --> 00:09:11,429
The disposal form, the GAO said, didn't

255
00:09:11,449 --> 00:09:13,626
show who destroyed them, when, or under

256
00:09:13,646 --> 00:09:14,471
what authority.

257
00:09:14,941 --> 00:09:17,020
The records center's chief archivist said

258
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:18,811
that happened often in that period.

259
00:09:19,381 --> 00:09:21,617
The Air Force itself admitted it found no

260
00:09:21,637 --> 00:09:23,927
document explaining why the base announced

261
00:09:23,947 --> 00:09:25,742
a flying disc in the first place.

262
00:09:26,212 --> 00:09:28,497
And the link to Flight 4 rests on a

263
00:09:28,517 --> 00:09:31,066
journal entry, a scientist's opinion, a

264
00:09:31,086 --> 00:09:33,832
witness's memory and the 1947 press photos

265
00:09:33,852 --> 00:09:34,754
of the debris.

266
00:09:35,094 --> 00:09:37,357
The report cites no tag or serial number

267
00:09:37,377 --> 00:09:39,183
tying the debris to that flight.

268
00:09:39,753 --> 00:09:42,386
The GAO's own search turned up just two

269
00:09:42,406 --> 00:09:44,970
government records from 1947 about the

270
00:09:44,990 --> 00:09:45,378
crash.

271
00:09:45,718 --> 00:09:48,074
The base history, and the FBI teletype.

272
00:09:48,994 --> 00:09:51,019
So, what does this file actually prove?

273
00:09:51,639 --> 00:09:54,006
It proves that in July 1947, the Army

274
00:09:54,026 --> 00:09:56,586
announced it had a flying disc, and took

275
00:09:56,606 --> 00:09:57,941
it back within a day.

276
00:09:58,411 --> 00:10:00,755
And that a Top Secret balloon project was

277
00:10:00,775 --> 00:10:02,772
flying over New Mexico at the time.

278
00:10:03,342 --> 00:10:05,492
It proves that the Air Force, searching

279
00:10:05,512 --> 00:10:07,550
its records nearly fifty years later,

280
00:10:07,570 --> 00:10:09,775
found nothing describing a crashed craft

281
00:10:09,795 --> 00:10:10,887
or recovered bodies.

282
00:10:11,357 --> 00:10:13,233
And it proves that some records that might

283
00:10:13,253 --> 00:10:14,587
have helped were already gone.

284
00:10:15,158 --> 00:10:17,094
What it doesn't prove matters just as

285
00:10:17,114 --> 00:10:17,359
much.

286
00:10:17,779 --> 00:10:20,011
The Air Force's Mogul answer is a best

287
00:10:20,031 --> 00:10:22,381
match, in its own words, the most likely

288
00:10:22,401 --> 00:10:22,796
source.

289
00:10:23,378 --> 00:10:25,763
And its explanation for the bodies depends

290
00:10:25,783 --> 00:10:28,169
on witnesses having misremembered dates by

291
00:10:28,189 --> 00:10:28,513
years.

292
00:10:28,933 --> 00:10:30,899
Many people still don't accept that.

293
00:10:31,469 --> 00:10:33,339
Every secret has a release date.

294
00:10:33,759 --> 00:10:36,003
Mogul's came in the 1970s.

295
00:10:36,423 --> 00:10:39,554
Roswell's explanation took the Air Force

296
00:10:39,574 --> 00:10:40,421
until 1997.

297
00:10:41,004 --> 00:10:43,109
Whether it closed the case is still being

298
00:10:43,129 --> 00:10:43,472
argued.

299
00:10:44,291 --> 00:10:46,251
If there's a government file you want us

300
00:10:46,271 --> 00:10:47,884
to open, tell us in the comments.

301
00:10:48,454 --> 00:10:50,499
Next time: the photographs that took the

302
00:10:50,519 --> 00:10:52,202
world to the edge of nuclear war.
